# Rootless touchscreen toggle on the HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 2025 (FMB-P).
# Grant the `input` group write access to the REAL FTSC1000 multitouch node's
# `inhibited` attr (exact name match — the bogus "... UNKNOWN" sibling is
# force-inhibited by 99-honor-fmbp-touchscreen.rules and must stay that way) so
# honor-fmbp-touchscreen-toggle can flip it without root. sysfs attrs can't take
# systemd's uaccess ACLs (those are devnode-only), so group+g+w is the packaged
# mechanism; users not in `input` fall back to the script's pkexec path.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="FTSC1000:00 2808:5662", RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'chgrp input /sys$env{DEVPATH}/../inhibited && chmod g+w /sys$env{DEVPATH}/../inhibited'"
